<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔρῑπος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>any strait</i> or <i>narrow sea,
				where the flux and reflux is violent</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				1.6.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				544a21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				548a9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mu.</u>
				396a25
			</span></i>; esp. <i>the strait which separates Euboea from Boeotia,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Ap.
				222
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.77
			</span></i>, etc., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.2.8
			</span></i>: prov. of <i>an unstable, weak-minded</i> person (cf.
				<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				6.121
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλείους τραπόμενος τροπὰς τοῦ Εὐρίπου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					3.90
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταρρεῖ ὥσπερ Εὔριπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1167b7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστατα καὶ ἀβέβαια Εὐρίπου τρόπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hipparch.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.44.81
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὔριποι γενόμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lib.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					907
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> generally,
				<i>canal, ditch</i>, etc., <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				799.7
			</span></i> (Cyzicus, <span class="entity">i A.D.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				120.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				14.135.2
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Metrod.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				3.68
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> the
				<u>Spina</u> in the Circus, <i><span class="en">
				Lyd.
				<u>Mens.</u>
				1.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>ventilator, fan</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ εὐρίπου τινὸς αὔραν εἰσπνεῖν
					ἐπιτεχνώμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					10.649
				</span></i>
			. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖ, ῥιπή,
		ῥιπίζω</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
